Once the media fanout is up, answer relay-latency probes only for the relays it connected to.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, on top of 0002 (upstream PR #26) and 0004.

Why: onRelayLatency endorses every relay in the offer. The caller probes twice, once
while ringing and again about a second after accept (seen in the spike logs of
fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#235: fanout established at 13:01:13, second probe round
at 13:01:14), and the second round is what elects the relay its media moves to. A
relay that failed to connect, or that 0004 left out for missing its 2 s grace, was
still endorsed then, and electing it silences inbound audio while another relay is
connected. runMedia now records the relays the fanout holds, and onRelayLatency
answers only for those once they exist; before the fanout, it still answers for the
offered ones, which is all there is to go on while ringing.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387 (rounds 1, 7 and 8); tracked
as fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#388.

